Carried patch on third_party/bwapi (bwapi/bwapi @ d727fed68558c506163048ea889131d8cbb33915).
Plan: docs/c-abi-plan.md section 15.2; docs/pins.md.

BWAPIClient/Source/Convenience.h:33 takes `va_list &ap`. MSVC's va_list is `char*`, so a
reference binds; glibc's is an array type and cannot, which blocks GameImpl.cpp on every
non-MSVC compiler (R6 section 5). Taking it by value is layout-neutral and what vsnprintf
wants anyway. Needed for the Linux-native test suite (plan section 11).

Upstream issue: not yet filed.

